#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059522 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1fe5d8aa-8a79-5de4-8566-1432a640d78f" :knowledge-point/title "Equating Real and Imaginary Parts of a Complex Number to Solve For an Unknown Quantity"}] :question/id #uuid "fbe381a7-e6fb-52c1-bfdb-b77fd90a4b6a" :question/math-academy-id "e-5245" :question/problem "Given that $3+2\\textrm{i} = a + \\textrm{i}b,$ calculate the value of $a$ and the value of $b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we equate the real parts:\n\n$$\n3 = a\n$$\n\nThen, we equate the imaginary parts:\n\n$$\n2 = b\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=3$ and $b=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059524 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1bbe2fe7-b69c-54f3-9f1c-3369e3f1395d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Unknowns By Computing a Product and Equating Real and Imaginary Parts"}] :question/id #uuid "17e0ddb4-5a70-586b-9eec-e1cb584418e2" :question/math-academy-id "e-5261" :question/problem "Given that $2 - 3 \\textrm{i} = \\dfrac{p - 2q \\textrm{i} }{1 + 2 \\textrm{i}},$ calculate $p$ and $q.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $1+2\\textrm{i}$ to get rid of the fraction and isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-3\\text{i} & =\\frac{p-2q\\text{i}}{1+2\\text{i}} \\\\ (2-3\\text{i})(1+2\\text{i}) & =p-2q\\text{i} \\\\ 2+4\\text{i}-3\\text{i}-6{\\text{i}}^{2} & =p-2q\\text{i} \\\\ 2+\\text{i}-6(-1) & =p-2q\\text{i} \\\\ 8+\\text{i} & =p-2q\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get\n\n$$\n8 = p.\n$$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =-2q \\\\ q & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=8$ and $q = -\\dfrac{1}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059525 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c9f40a0e-83f3-5814-b9a1-8b1265fe93cc" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Unknowns By Computing a Quotient and Equating Real and Imaginary Parts"}] :question/id #uuid "746b590e-3b43-5de2-92fc-97ae7826c1fa" :question/math-academy-id "e-5293" :question/problem "Given that $3+5\\textrm{i} = (p+\\textrm{i}q)(1+\\textrm{i}),$ calculate $p$ and $q.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we divide both sides of the equation by $1+\\textrm{i}$ to isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3+5\\text{i} & =(p+\\text{i}q)(1+\\text{i}) \\\\ \\frac{3+5\\text{i}}{1+\\text{i}} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to simplify the fraction on the left-hand side, we multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(3+5\\text{i})(1-\\text{i})}{(1+\\text{i})(1-\\text{i})} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{3-3\\text{i}+5\\text{i}-5{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{1}^{2}-{\\text{i}}^{2}} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{3+2\\text{i}-5(-1)}{1-(-1)} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{8+2\\text{i}}{2} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ 4+\\text{i} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get $4=p.$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get $1=q.$\n\nTherefore, $p=4$ and $q=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313446 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1fe5d8aa-8a79-5de4-8566-1432a640d78f" :knowledge-point/title "Equating Real and Imaginary Parts of a Complex Number to Solve For an Unknown Quantity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d201c5d2-33ed-5990-b470-be15c705c915" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=\\frac{3}{4},b=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313448} {:answer/id #uuid "3614b769-db41-5c49-ae9f-ccff7e405e2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=\\sqrt{3},b=-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313449} {:answer/id #uuid "0f932ffe-5c1e-5585-ae54-dffe1e49f0ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=\\frac{3}{4},b=-\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313450} {:answer/id #uuid "35e9d7bc-115d-5eef-b28b-7d93d7a55ccc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=\\sqrt{3},b=\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313451} {:answer/id #uuid "7d454b21-8cae-51d7-8e5c-7886af7b299d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=\\frac{3}{4},b=\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313452}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d454b21-8cae-51d7-8e5c-7886af7b299d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=\\frac{3}{4},b=\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313452} :answer-field/id #uuid "441caaff-8709-5b6c-b57d-974573fa490f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313447}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "78111624-f670-5df8-b6e2-bb5a5dde19ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-160013" :question/problem "Given that $\\frac{3}{4}+\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}=a+b\\text{i}$, calculate the value of $a$ and the value of $b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we equate the real parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4} & =a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we equate the imaginary parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & =b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=\\frac{3}{4}$ and $b=\\sqrt{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313453 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1bbe2fe7-b69c-54f3-9f1c-3369e3f1395d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Unknowns By Computing a Product and Equating Real and Imaginary Parts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46bbb13c-ab62-57bc-9023-58dd905ed711" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=-2,q=-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313455} {:answer/id #uuid "92fa84e7-8288-5fe8-88e2-2c3b2c32e2c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=-2,q=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313456} {:answer/id #uuid "5d50f5ac-1165-5b25-8272-dbd5d92ba7ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=-1,q=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313457} {:answer/id #uuid "03ca134f-54ff-51be-9740-1b6a99a86ec2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=-1,q=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313458} {:answer/id #uuid "4807703d-ea87-5aad-a030-79582c32c7dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=-4,q=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313459}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46bbb13c-ab62-57bc-9023-58dd905ed711" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=-2,q=-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313455} :answer-field/id #uuid "f67d1dfe-3a13-519d-8ab9-ea6af168825e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313454}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1273a17f-9601-5e3d-93d7-d4842c398726" :question/math-academy-id "q-160043" :question/problem "Given that $-4+\\text{i}=\\frac{p+\\text{i}q}{2\\text{i}},$ calculate $p$ and $q.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $2\\text{i}$ to get rid of the fraction and isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4+\\text{i} & =\\frac{p+\\text{i}q}{2\\text{i}} \\\\ (-4+\\text{i})(2\\text{i}) & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ -8\\text{i}+2{\\text{i}}^{2} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ -2-8\\text{i} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get\n\n$$\n-2=p.\n$$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-8 & =q.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=-2$ and $q=-8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313460 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c9f40a0e-83f3-5814-b9a1-8b1265fe93cc" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Unknowns By Computing a Quotient and Equating Real and Imaginary Parts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45c8b7f2-9be5-55b5-a22b-e054f4cbe1af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=-\\frac{3}{2},q=\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313462} {:answer/id #uuid "ba57b036-ebae-511e-91ae-a387bf1362b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=\\frac{3}{2},q=-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313463} {:answer/id #uuid "f1d591eb-6b58-5f15-9e36-44f9420dc798" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=\\frac{3}{5},q=-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313464} {:answer/id #uuid "8c53c1c6-f880-529f-9ea9-1db90afcb2e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=\\frac{2}{5},q=-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313465} {:answer/id #uuid "c4270e82-24f8-5ea2-8d59-88b154a06aeb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=\\frac{3}{2},q=-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313466}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4270e82-24f8-5ea2-8d59-88b154a06aeb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=\\frac{3}{2},q=-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313466} :answer-field/id #uuid "37604755-f009-5aae-942f-1a1f1e4a3997" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313461}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "050685d3-106a-556e-94cf-f2ab6b33d435" :question/math-academy-id "q-160049" :question/problem "Given that $5=(p+q\\text{i})(3+\\text{i})$, calculate $p$ and $q.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we divide both sides of the equation by $3+\\text{i}$ to isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =(p+q\\text{i})(3+\\text{i}) \\\\ \\frac{5}{3+\\text{i}} & =p+q\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to simplify the fraction on the left-hand side, we multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(5)(3-\\text{i})}{(3+\\text{i})(3-\\text{i})} & =p+q\\text{i} \\\\ \\frac{15-5\\text{i}}{{3}^{2}-(\\text{i})^{2}} & =p+q\\text{i} \\\\ \\frac{15-5\\text{i}}{9+1} & =p+q\\text{i} \\\\ \\frac{15-5\\text{i}}{10} & =p+q\\text{i} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\text{i} & =p+q\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get $\\frac{3}{2}=p.$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get $-\\frac{1}{2}=q.$\n\nTherefore, $p=\\frac{3}{2}$ and $q=-\\frac{1}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313467 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c9f40a0e-83f3-5814-b9a1-8b1265fe93cc" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Unknowns By Computing a Quotient and Equating Real and Imaginary Parts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7a7c332-9fb8-5488-b6aa-7afa28cd75c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=-1,q=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313469} {:answer/id #uuid "51f1a684-8ad3-553d-9551-edb51a5e4097" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=1,q=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313470} {:answer/id #uuid "c7f28ec3-5678-5756-ac7e-708b04a20a9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=2,q=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313471} {:answer/id #uuid "8a1d09b0-d145-5d5e-9776-9d4f5468cd5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=-2,q=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313472} {:answer/id #uuid "6070670a-3387-5464-9508-e4edb16634d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=-1,q=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313473}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7a7c332-9fb8-5488-b6aa-7afa28cd75c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=-1,q=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313469} :answer-field/id #uuid "97a5ea3f-9e83-58d6-9b5b-e34e8edd2ed5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313468}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "77d9662b-7262-5332-935d-549a31e7f0a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-160050" :question/problem "Given that $1+7\\text{i}=(p+\\text{i}q)(3-4\\text{i})$, calculate $p$ and $q.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we divide both sides of the equation by $3-4\\text{i}$ to isolate the\n  variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+7\\text{i} & =(p+\\text{i}q)(3-4\\text{i}) \\\\ \\frac{1+7\\text{i}}{3-4\\text{i}} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to simplify the fraction on the left-hand side, we multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(1+7\\text{i})(3+4\\text{i})}{(3-4\\text{i})(3+4\\text{i})} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{3+21\\text{i}+4\\text{i}+28{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{3}^{2}-(4\\text{i})^{2}} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{-25+25\\text{i}}{9+16} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{-25+25\\text{i}}{25} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ -1+\\text{i} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get $-1=p.$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get $1=q.$\n\nTherefore, $p=-1$ and $q=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313474 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1bbe2fe7-b69c-54f3-9f1c-3369e3f1395d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Unknowns By Computing a Product and Equating Real and Imaginary Parts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fb50973-a875-53c7-b698-6e8764a19d60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p=-\\frac{3}{4}$, $q=\\frac{3}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313476} {:answer/id #uuid "02e5ebcf-50d7-5d71-9668-bcad2ca5ccf3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p=-3$, $q=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313477} {:answer/id #uuid "de98f9bd-100b-526c-96d1-fa7979cc37a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p=\\frac{4}{3}$, $q=-\\frac{1}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313478} {:answer/id #uuid "fcb8b0bd-5c8a-530e-99f7-ae9b14a3b6ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p=\\frac{8}{3}$, $q=\\frac{1}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313479} {:answer/id #uuid "1f5561fe-a8ca-5906-a1ec-9766b8e26c10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p=-4$, $q=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313480}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fcb8b0bd-5c8a-530e-99f7-ae9b14a3b6ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p=\\frac{8}{3}$, $q=\\frac{1}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313479} :answer-field/id #uuid "a48499cc-b2a7-581d-a6cd-4e0b0ec06a8e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313475}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9dabd258-08a3-5975-8674-6e9f1bd600ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-16552" :question/problem "Given that $\\frac{3p+2q\\text{i}}{2-3\\text{i}}=1+2\\text{i}$, calculate $p$ and $q.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $2-3\\text{i}$ to get rid of the fraction and isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3p+2q\\text{i}}{2-3\\text{i}} & =1+2\\text{i} \\\\ 3p+2q\\text{i} & =(1+2\\text{i})(2-3\\text{i}) \\\\ 3p+2q\\text{i} & =2-3\\text{i}+4\\text{i}-6{\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\ 3p+2q\\text{i} & =2+\\text{i}-6(-1) \\\\ 3p+2q\\text{i} & =8+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3p & =8 \\\\ p & =\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2q & =1 \\\\ q & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=\\frac{8}{3}$ and $q=\\frac{1}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313481 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1bbe2fe7-b69c-54f3-9f1c-3369e3f1395d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Unknowns By Computing a Product and Equating Real and Imaginary Parts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb8909ea-3d4a-5901-98ff-99851ac32a34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313483} {:answer/id #uuid "91d4dccc-27c6-51a4-b54f-1bc0468fd8f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313484}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91d4dccc-27c6-51a4-b54f-1bc0468fd8f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313484} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed68bc47-c290-5df5-bb0f-473aa53e7443" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313482} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dbcf42e3-62bb-53a9-b3cf-d54527113087" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313486}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbcf42e3-62bb-53a9-b3cf-d54527113087" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313486} :answer-field/id #uuid "c78e8003-b7ca-58de-a2db-f7d083140417" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313485}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c49dd4d9-a6cd-5226-8787-0dd1f2c141a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-275089" :question/problem "If  $6-\\text{i}=\\frac{p+q\\text{i}}{2+3\\text{i}},$ then$\\,p=$\n{{field-1}}\nand\n$q=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $2+3\\text{i}$ to get rid of the fraction and isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6-\\text{i}=\\frac{p+q\\text{i}}{2+3\\text{i}} \\\\ (6-\\text{i})(2+3\\text{i}) & =p+q\\text{i} \\\\ 12+18\\text{i}-2\\text{i}-3{\\text{i}}^{2} & =p+q\\text{i} \\\\ 12+3+16\\text{i} & =p+q\\text{i} \\\\ 15+16\\text{i} & =p+q\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get\n\n$$\n15=p.\n$$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16 & =q.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=15$ and $q=16.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313487 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c9f40a0e-83f3-5814-b9a1-8b1265fe93cc" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Unknowns By Computing a Quotient and Equating Real and Imaginary Parts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39a9c4f1-d473-518a-a950-2f61222073fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{32}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313489} {:answer/id #uuid "c0718f95-8035-5523-be2a-734012216cab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313490}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0718f95-8035-5523-be2a-734012216cab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313490} :answer-field/id #uuid "80a7f906-2981-596b-9a0a-6538b3776ea3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313488} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5198a42b-e7f3-5abb-9d87-3f5adab37bcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{65}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313492}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5198a42b-e7f3-5abb-9d87-3f5adab37bcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{65}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313492} :answer-field/id #uuid "4056c54e-298f-5c3e-a5ee-89c1961d9f79" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313491}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6b34ee7b-9dc7-52b2-9d59-2025071a0239" :question/math-academy-id "q-280406" :question/problem "Given that $\\frac{6-7\\text{i}}{3-2\\text{i}}=2p-5q\\text{i}$, then$\\,p=$\n{{field-1}}\nand\n$q=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, to simplify the fraction on the left-hand side, we multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6-7\\text{i}}{3-2\\text{i}} & =2p-5q\\text{i} \\\\ \\frac{(6-7\\text{i})(3+2\\text{i})}{(3-2\\text{i})(3+2\\text{i})} & =2p-5q\\text{i} \\\\ \\frac{18+12\\text{i}-21\\text{i}-14{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}} & =2p-5q\\text{i} \\\\ \\frac{18-9\\text{i}-14(-1)}{13} & =2p-5q\\text{i} \\\\ \\frac{32-9\\text{i}}{13} & =2p-5q\\text{i} \\\\ \\frac{32}{13}-\\frac{9}{13}\\text{i} & =2p-5q\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get $\\frac{32}{13}=2p.$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get $-\\frac{9}{13}=-5q.$\n\nTherefore, $p=\\frac{16}{13}$ and $q=\\frac{9}{65}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313493 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1fe5d8aa-8a79-5de4-8566-1432a640d78f" :knowledge-point/title "Equating Real and Imaginary Parts of a Complex Number to Solve For an Unknown Quantity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b51e5aab-c2f6-58b9-8689-5937f9d5785f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313495} {:answer/id #uuid "db4778f5-fd9a-59a8-98c4-f0229ba17347" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313496}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b51e5aab-c2f6-58b9-8689-5937f9d5785f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313495} :answer-field/id #uuid "d73a2b30-769d-541b-a81a-1a389f2f4bf2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313494} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd704096-0cb6-5e0f-84be-126c5f50d5e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313498}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd704096-0cb6-5e0f-84be-126c5f50d5e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313498} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7569ce0-9225-52cf-90fa-1c3624be43eb" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313497}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f0886e3c-adae-5fca-9557-3a5ce4689d1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-280572" :question/problem "If $-7+6\\text{i}=a+b\\text{i}$, then$\\,a=$\n{{field-1}}\nand\n$b=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we equate the real parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7 & =a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we equate the imaginary parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6 & =b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-7$ and $b=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313499 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1fe5d8aa-8a79-5de4-8566-1432a640d78f" :knowledge-point/title "Equating Real and Imaginary Parts of a Complex Number to Solve For an Unknown Quantity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7988ca2-482d-5101-8787-45c6f2fa9f81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313501}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7988ca2-482d-5101-8787-45c6f2fa9f81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313501} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e6d2620-fe3a-575a-ba88-1d9684207c55" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313500} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "450f2b2e-69c7-59ba-aacb-ca18991aa697" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313503}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "450f2b2e-69c7-59ba-aacb-ca18991aa697" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313503} :answer-field/id #uuid "0cbe6966-7990-54d8-a9ce-9a775583a065" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313502}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "77a56348-f84b-5d57-9641-9b5b6da0e05a" :question/math-academy-id "q-280585" :question/problem "If  $\\sqrt{5}+6\\text{i}=a+b\\text{i}$,  then$\\,a=$\n{{field-1}}\nand\n$b=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we equate the real parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & =a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we equate the imaginary parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6 & =b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=\\sqrt{5}$ and $b=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313504 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1fe5d8aa-8a79-5de4-8566-1432a640d78f" :knowledge-point/title "Equating Real and Imaginary Parts of a Complex Number to Solve For an Unknown Quantity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bf3feef-f621-5ca4-865e-b35f0a381d72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=\\sqrt{3}$, $b=-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313506} {:answer/id #uuid "1b6f8ef3-3459-5a03-a87d-e84d5601c7b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=-2$, $b=\\sqrt{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313507} {:answer/id #uuid "a049403c-0945-5c8a-9f59-810ff01734ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=\\sqrt{3}$, $b=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313508} {:answer/id #uuid "9ef9d8ce-ae77-5aca-8390-2934b291aeb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=-\\sqrt{3}$, $b=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313509} {:answer/id #uuid "7aa56be7-0839-5f2d-ab93-1f9161c60cbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=1+\\sqrt{3}$, $b=-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313510}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0bf3feef-f621-5ca4-865e-b35f0a381d72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=\\sqrt{3}$, $b=-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313506} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7e7159e-e4e2-5094-8edc-e4789968483d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313505}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2d09c741-59f7-5ee4-8327-aa9511717b30" :question/math-academy-id "q-70797" :question/problem "Given that $\\sqrt{3}-2\\text{i}=a+b\\text{i}$, calculate the value of $a$ and the value of $b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we equate the real parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & =a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we equate the imaginary parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2 & =b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=\\sqrt{3}$ and $b=-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313511 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1fe5d8aa-8a79-5de4-8566-1432a640d78f" :knowledge-point/title "Equating Real and Imaginary Parts of a Complex Number to Solve For an Unknown Quantity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "190bc793-9ae4-5ff3-a0bf-1410433f0416" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=1$, $b=-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313513} {:answer/id #uuid "8ac9a618-84c4-52eb-924e-7b3d2a172f53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=-1$, $b=-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313514} {:answer/id #uuid "47232b1b-abdd-5e3c-a62a-8a48a7d20030" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=i$, $b=-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313515} {:answer/id #uuid "7c777fec-7668-55d3-84ff-e00aa3e53289" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=1$, $b=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313516} {:answer/id #uuid "0c6ca0a1-9461-5538-8d62-833dacf66675" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=-1$, $b=-i$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313517}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ac9a618-84c4-52eb-924e-7b3d2a172f53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=-1$, $b=-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313514} :answer-field/id #uuid "7dec1858-006f-563e-8a14-a3e910124451" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313512}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dcfb236d-9ae7-5476-ab43-deea9de23185" :question/math-academy-id "q-70799" :question/problem "Given that $-1-\\text{i}=a+b\\text{i}$, calculate the value of $a$ and the value of $b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we equate the real parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & =a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we equate the imaginary parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & =b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-1$ and $b=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060333 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c9f40a0e-83f3-5814-b9a1-8b1265fe93cc" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Unknowns By Computing a Quotient and Equating Real and Imaginary Parts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4a3d761-7dba-5cc8-974c-f1d934ac16a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p = 1$, $q =-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058982} {:answer/id #uuid "ecbfe6bb-6776-5984-bd78-49836b104618" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p =-3$, $q =-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058983} {:answer/id #uuid "1c77acd0-2324-555a-990a-d137c1c9d4fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p =-1$, $q =-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058984} {:answer/id #uuid "1e0914e8-0b54-5949-bad9-74f229fa4af9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p = \\frac{3}{2}$, $q =-\\frac{3}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058985} {:answer/id #uuid "592a59b3-8738-5092-b711-d565a43e8315" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p = 2$, $q =-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058986}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4a3d761-7dba-5cc8-974c-f1d934ac16a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p = 1$, $q =-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058982} :answer-field/id #uuid "b375e472-6115-5807-9575-7cb1605d670f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058981}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7075d093-3130-53bd-98c6-59bdcaa6e2bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-8036" :question/problem "Given that $5-\\text{i}=(p+\\text{i}q)(3+2\\text{i})$, calculate $p$ and $q.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we divide both sides of the equation by $3+2\\text{i}$ to isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5-\\text{i} & =(p+\\text{i}q)(3+2\\text{i}) \\\\ \\frac{5-\\text{i}}{3+2\\text{i}} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to simplify the fraction on the left-hand side, we multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(5-\\text{i})(3-2\\text{i})}{(3+2\\text{i})(3-2\\text{i})} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{15-3\\text{i}-10\\text{i}+2{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{3}^{2}-(2\\text{i})^{2}} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{13-13\\text{i}}{9+4} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{13-13\\text{i}}{13} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ 1-\\text{i} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get $1=p.$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get $-1=q.$\n\nTherefore, $p=1$ and $q=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060351 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c9f40a0e-83f3-5814-b9a1-8b1265fe93cc" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Unknowns By Computing a Quotient and Equating Real and Imaginary Parts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f741c71e-befa-5d0f-b026-df1cd168e239" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p=3$, $q=-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313519} {:answer/id #uuid "917c4db6-b341-58ff-ba46-14f05344deae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p=2$, $q=3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313520} {:answer/id #uuid "ea59a192-9ad0-57e4-918d-3e77cac380ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p=-5$, $q=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313521} {:answer/id #uuid "f972a3be-8786-59f6-bf96-15c2afdd48c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p=-3$, $q=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313522} {:answer/id #uuid "ed6ecd6c-28ca-5546-b66f-890e2dfb2a02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p=-1$, $q=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313523}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f972a3be-8786-59f6-bf96-15c2afdd48c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p=-3$, $q=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313522} :answer-field/id #uuid "7134303b-3280-56f4-98af-02b5c1ea53ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313518}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c5329687-3e1f-56b6-842b-a7b8acc29964" :question/math-academy-id "q-8407" :question/problem "Given that $\\frac{13\\text{i}}{2-3\\text{i}}=p+\\text{i}q,$ calculate $p$ and $q.$" :question/worked-solution "First, to simplify the fraction on the left-hand side, we multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{13\\text{i}(2+3\\text{i})}{(2-3\\text{i})(2+3\\text{i})} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{13\\text{i}(2+3\\text{i})}{(2)^{2}-(3\\text{i})^{2}} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{13\\text{i}(2+3\\text{i})}{13} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\text{i}(2+3\\text{i}) & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ 2\\text{i}+3{\\text{i}}^{2} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ -3+2\\text{i} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get $-3=p.$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get $2=q.$\n\nTherefore, $p=-3$ and $q=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313524 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1bbe2fe7-b69c-54f3-9f1c-3369e3f1395d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Unknowns By Computing a Product and Equating Real and Imaginary Parts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67081898-0835-5e62-8403-84093bb80e0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p=4$, $q=-6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313526} {:answer/id #uuid "4f72c1c1-4681-52d3-9806-924ac41c942b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p=-4$, $q=-6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313527} {:answer/id #uuid "d3c6a741-93f1-55c8-bea5-52582c7c35ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p=2$, $q=-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313528} {:answer/id #uuid "ad201510-e91e-5a79-a59b-fe01d0db7a1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p=6$, $q=-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313529} {:answer/id #uuid "f831ecd3-fa88-52c4-b269-76da2f26bc5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p=-6$, $q=-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313530}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67081898-0835-5e62-8403-84093bb80e0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p=4$, $q=-6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313526} :answer-field/id #uuid "fba79f83-12a3-5026-a958-4a08db991d3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313525}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "216ae57a-81ed-5f5e-b145-ffbb67f1cde3" :question/math-academy-id "q-8408" :question/problem "Given that $-3-2\\text{i}=\\frac{p+\\text{i}q}{2\\text{i}}$, calculate $p$ and $q.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $2\\text{i}$ to get rid of the fraction and isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3-2\\text{i} & =\\frac{p+\\text{i}q}{2\\text{i}} \\\\ 2\\text{i}(-3-2\\text{i}) & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ -6\\text{i}-4{\\text{i}}^{2} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ 4-6\\text{i} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get\n\n$$\n4=p.\n$$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6 & =q.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=4$ and $q=-6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313531 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1bbe2fe7-b69c-54f3-9f1c-3369e3f1395d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Unknowns By Computing a Product and Equating Real and Imaginary Parts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a545094-50fd-5a76-909c-15cbb359a2a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p=-4$, $q=-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313533} {:answer/id #uuid "c95d874b-a082-5c74-b132-481dcbda63be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p=\\frac{2}{5}$, $q=\\frac{4}{5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313534} {:answer/id #uuid "95a5a1f0-6169-5838-a450-3087c4f7d450" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p=5$, $q=4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313535} {:answer/id #uuid "5b1e9a44-349c-554e-aece-cab5090e5be3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p=\\frac{1}{5}$, $q=-\\,\\frac{3}{5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313536} {:answer/id #uuid "75de96a6-1dee-5fb7-b4dd-6f59a69acba3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p=1$, $q=-\\,\\frac{3}{5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95a5a1f0-6169-5838-a450-3087c4f7d450" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p=5$, $q=4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313535} :answer-field/id #uuid "e45da950-da9c-5489-bd7a-dc764d54a054" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313532}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "196e7c79-56bb-55f4-85a9-98019ba4d55e" :question/math-academy-id "q-8412" :question/problem "Given that $\\frac{6+13\\text{i}}{5}=\\frac{p+\\text{i}q}{2-\\text{i}}$, calculate $p$ and $q.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $2-\\text{i}$ to get rid of the fraction and isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6+13\\text{i}}{5} & =\\frac{p+\\text{i}q}{2-\\text{i}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}(6+13\\text{i})(2-\\text{i}) & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}(12-6\\text{i}+26\\text{i}-13{\\text{i}}^{2}) & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}(12+13+20\\text{i}) & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}(25+20\\text{i}) & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ 5+4\\text{i} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get\n\n$$\n5=p.\n$$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =q.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=5$ and $q=4.$"}]}
